{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrzp2FuZLkoLtDfAqjHQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The root cause was mutable default arguments in `inv/warehouse.py`, and I fixed it there. The one test in the repo (`tests/test_inv.py`) passes now. It's the only test, so nothing else was checked.\n\n- **`Warehouse.__init__`:** `stock={}` and `history=[]` were created once and shared by every `Warehouse` built without arguments. That's why a second warehouse showed the first one's stock and why `restock` on one changed another. Both now default to `None` and each instance gets its own fresh dict and list. If a caller passes their own, it's used as before.\n- **`Warehouse.restock`:** `tags=[]` had the same bug. Every new item created without tags shared one list, so tagging one item would have tagged the others. It now defaults to `None`, and the item gets its own copy of any tags passed in.\n\nThe `restock` change goes beyond the reported symptoms, but it's the same bug in the same file. I didn't change the test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9434,"cache_read_input_tokens":35089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9434},"output_tokens":314,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e6f38e4-5bbd-4779-b497-fbbbf0dd1b60","uuid":"0a23a133-3590-4d63-b599-c78fa44e98f9","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:42:42.002Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrzp1xZBTBUu2JRJF3oF"}
